<title>USA: Fair skies dominate Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</title>
<headline>Fair skies dominate Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Warm, high pressure aloft over Brazil's coffee belt is expected to remain in place through the coming weekend, Weather Services Corp said in an update on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Colder weather building in Argentina is expected to move through the coffee belt between now and Saturday, but the high pressure system already in place should prevent the cooler air from affecting the region, according to WSC.</p>
<p>Fair skies once again dominated the coffee belt yesterday. Temperatures remained near to above normal with lows ranging between 55-63 F (13-17 C).</p>
<p>Mostly fair weather is expected for today and Thursday. There is a slight chance of showers developing in southern areas of the belt on Friday. Mostly fair skies are expected to return through Monday. The lowest temperatures throughout the period will remain above 50 F (10 C).</p>
<p>&quot;There is no frost or freeze in sight,&quot; WSC said.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
</text>
